From 700078a3c12eaf648af0229ff8aca7ae52f23669 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:44:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] dwc2d: hub drop diagnosis and recovery, no sleep (#151)

A hub port that changed, lost its enable bit, went over current or lost
power is logged with its status and change bits, the change bits are
cleared, and a port without power is switched on again. A port whose
device fails to enumerate gets three more tries. A disabled root port
starts the enumeration over. Channel errors are counted by kind and
written with the port events to /tmp/dwc2d-usbstats after every rescan;
/tmp/dwc2d-step names the hotplug step dwc2d is in.

dwc2d no longer calls sleep: a nanosleep sometimes never returned (50 us
sleeps hung dwc2d in QEMU; on the Pi it stopped right after a hub drop,
test 168). delay() yields until the time has passed.
